// ProjectDeliveryS667 — Sprint 667: The suite receipt and the touched receipt say the same thing with the same words: at is the moment the receipt was WRITTEN - the end of a done run, the start of a running stub - and seconds is the run's wall clock (D0442, resolving issue472). Until now suite.rs stamped at with the launch epoch on both the stub and the done receipt, so a verifier checking at against its own launch learned the run's identity and never its completion, and the test-verify skill taught a filesystem workaround (the receipt's mtime minus at) for a quantity the touched receipt states in a field.. EXECUTE. 2 pts.
