    verification receiptAtMeansTheSameInBothReceiptsImplementGate : Test { :>> id = "6bbce501-6b7e-489e-a307-bfe7e5ae67ed"; :>> title = "Sprint 667 implement gate"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-11"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "keel-cli/src/suite.rs: Receipt.seconds; parse_receipt reads seconds defaulting 0; render_receipt writes seconds and its header states what at means; the stub carries seconds 0; the done receipt is done_receipt(fp, head, started, now_secs(), passed, failed, outcome); two new unit tests beside a_running_stub_is_not_green_and_a_killed_run_leaves_it. .engine/skills/test-verify/SKILL.md: the SUITE clause reads seconds and states the shared meaning of at. scripts/exec_brief/facts.py: suiteWallMinutes from seconds when present, mtime fallback named as the pre-issue472 shape. .engine/decisions/0442. No guard, hook or CI file moves."; }
